WHAT CHANGED IN v1.9 (the hub now checks its own work)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Every click used to be counted as a success whether or not the game actually
did anything, so the counters could not be trusted and dead buttons were
hammered forever. Now:

* VERIFIED WORK. After every action the hub fingerprints the game's own
  on-screen numbers, then re-reads them a moment later. Unchanged means the
  click did nothing.
* HONEST COUNTERS. The number beside each mode is its attempts; a mode that
  has been confirmed shows green, one that is clicking with no effect in the
  game turns amber, and the log says so by name. SCAN prints attempts and
  confirmations per mode.
* SMART PATIENCE. A target that does nothing is retried less and less often
  (2.5s up to 30s) so it stops stealing the click budget from modes that are
  working. One confirmed result resets it immediately.
* COOLDOWNS CAN NO LONGE BE SHORTENED. Every per-target cooldown is written
  through one function that can only raise a deadline, so a backoff can never
  undo the 90s gamepass shelve or the 30s stuck shelve.
* CORRECT TOOL IN HAND. The hub remembers the exact tool it equipped and will
  put away that tool (never one you or the game equipped) when moving to a
  mode that needs a different one.
* A banner after loading reports how many things it found, or tells you to
  walk to your base.

